  "title": "A disposition to have a higher-order thought is not enough",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "1f4ca5b4-383c-4892-b47c-3f8498f5f512",
      "text": "Against Carruthers' dispositional variant, being disposed to have a thought about a state does not make one conscious of it, so only an occurrent higher-order thought satisfies the transitivity principle.",
